Z||000000||overlord||07-10-2000||01:54 PM||||i called this guy about a 87 fiero GT a weeek ago...adn he mentioned it was an auto with 3 speed with overdrive.<P>did fieros come with overdrive from the factory??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-10-2000||02:15 PM||||Fieros never came with an automatic overdrive.<BR>He's probably talking about the bump that he feels when the TCC locks up. Actually feels like a shift. And the revs drop a little bit, too. <P>Unless someone's swapped in a 3800...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-10-2000||02:23 PM||||Actually, you can replace the TH125 with a later model OD transmission. There has been a lot of discussion on the topic in the past. However, no one on this forum has actually "stepped up to the plate" with specific details other than saying one axle has to be shortened. <P>I was really interested in this conversion a few months ago but wound up selling my 87 GT auto to my brother-in-law and bought an 87 GT 5-speed. I would still like to find out more beacuse he has already hinted about converting the car to an OD transmission.<P>You may want to call the guy back and ask for more specific information to see if it just the TH125 going into lockout or indeed it has been converted.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy||||reg||7
Z||000003||Raydar||07-10-2000||02:48 PM||||I've seen a car that Ed Parks swapped a 4T60 into, in conjunction with a 3.4. (Originally was a Duck.) Seems like he said it was a "pain in the a$$". Looked like it belonged there, though. <BR>I hope to do a 4T60 at some point. If I ever get around to doing it, I'll post plenty of pics. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||webbee||07-10-2000||03:59 PM||||I have an 84 duck w/auto & the auto's crapped, so, I am also interested in this swap. I was hopeing that someone would post something on this swap. Any body with pic's/info?||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||07-10-2000||06:40 PM||||If you go with a THM440C or 4T60 (non-E trans), it should go in fine but I believe the inner CV's need to be matched by using the 440's housing and the 125C spider. All 440C/4T60x trans use the HD axles and CV's and are 115mm bolt. You will likely need to swap the inner CV housing on the 125C inner CV's.<P>If you decide to go this route, find a remanufactured 440 or 4T60. They are nothing but 125C's with an overdrive spliced on and they had problems with them. The reman'd 440 or 4T60's have all of the updates and work much better and longer.<P>There are several final drives too, so pick one that suits your needs.<P>I've swapped them into other cars and this is what was necessary. VERIFY EVERYTHING FIRST!<P>1. Get a 440/4T60 preferably from a 2.8L/3.1L engine with a VSS sender and not a speedo cable although most can be swapped over from cable to VSS sender.<P>2. Get the 440/4T60 torque converter.<P>3. Get the 440/4T60 trans mounts (housing to rubber mounts).<P>4. Get the connectors for the TCC and PRNDL switch. The P/N and backup lights are on the trans.<P>5. Get the inner CV housings. You may need to you them with the inner CV spiders.<P>6. Get the block to trans bracket and TCC/flexplate cover.<P>7. Get the steel lines from the trans to the cooler hoses.<P>8. Get new axle output shaft seals, trans seal (where the input shaft goes in), and spline o-ring. Replace them all. Replace the filter too.<P>9. Replace the side cover gasket. While in there, remove the TCC solenoid and clean it out. <P>10. Replace all fluid with Dextron III.<P>11. Get the vacuum modulator and vaccum line that goes back up to the induction. You will need to add then in.<P>That's about all I can offer at this point.<P>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-10-2000||07:56 PM||||what he is feeling IS the TCC sel. I thought that I HAD  OD myself a week or so ago and unplugged the TCC and just tied it up to the air cleaner..... and it didn't (socalled) downshift...  then got the downshift as before... all it is is the TCC sel.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
